streak to nine games.","story":"TORONTO -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3899972/zach-werenski\">Zach Werenski</a> scored with 3:28 left in regulation as the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/cbj/columbus-blue-jackets\">Columbus Blue Jackets</a> battled back late to top Toronto 4-3 on Saturday night and extend the Maple Leafs’ winless streak to nine games.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5136617/adam-fantilli\">Adam Fantilli</a>, with a goal and an assist, <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3068087/damon-severson\">Damon Severson</a> and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4874919/matthew-knies\">Matthew Knies</a> provided the rest of the offense for Columbus (9-12-0), which got 23 saves from <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5734/cam-talbot\">Cam Talbot</a>. Werenski added an assist for a two-point night.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4024123/auston-matthews\">Auston Matthews</a>, <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3020803/jake-mccabe\">Jake McCabe</a> and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3024916/teddy-blueger\">Teddy Blueger</a> scored for Toronto (8-14-3). <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3067313/anthony-stolarz\">Anthony Stolarz</a> made 31 stops.\n\n\r\n              The Maple Leafs are now 0-8-1 over their last nine, including Thursday’s blown 3-0 lead against the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/la/los-angeles-kings\">Los Angeles Kings</a> that ended in a 4-3 shootout loss, and have won just one of their previous 12 games (1-10-1).\n\n\r\n              The Blue Jackets have won two straight after beating the Blackhawks 4-2 in Chicago on Thursday.\n\n\r\n              Maple Leafs winger <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3114736/william-nylander\">William Nylander</a> turned the puck over with under five minutes to go in regulation in his own zone before Knies scored against his former team to tie the game 3-3.\n\n\r\n              Winger <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4587996/kirill-marchenko\">Kirill Marchenko</a>, who was acquired from Columbus on the eve of the regular season, took part in Saturday’s morning skate sporting a red non-contact jersey as he continues to recover from a lower-body injury suffered Oct. 26.\n\n\r\n              Knies, who was part of the package going the other way for Marchenko in late September, suited up for the first time as a visitor at Scotiabank Arena. The big forward played 240 games for Toronto across parts of four seasons, including a career-high 66 points in 2025-26.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Blue Jackets: At New Jersey on Monday.\n\n\r\n              Maple Leafs: At the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/nyi/new-york-islanders\">New York Islanders</a> on Monday.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              \r\n                <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/nhl\">See AP’s full NHL coverage here</a>","published":"2026-11-22T03:13:33Z"}}